    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d157-a1">

                <pb facs="0289" n="195" sameAs="frus:frus1924v02/pg195"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Enclosure]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The British Secretary of State for Foreign
                        Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">MacDonald</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the American Ambassador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Kellogg</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1924-07-29"><hi rendition="#italic">July 29,
                        1924</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. W5896/23/98</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Your Excellency</hi>: You recently enquired whether
                    His Majesty’s Government were in a position to reply to Your Excellency’s note
                        <pb facs="0290" n="196" xml:id="pg196"/> of the 18th February last<anchor
                        n="9" xml:id="d157-f1"/> regarding the proposed treaties affecting the
                    former German territories in Central Africa now administered by His Majesty’s
                    Government under mandate on behalf of the League of Nations, and to proceed to
                    the conclusion of those treaties.</p>
                <p>2. I have the honor to state that His Majesty’s Government would prefer to
                    postpone their final answer to the note in question until a more advanced stage
                    has been reached in the negotiation of the treaty relating to the British
                    mandate in Palestine. Their views on the latest proposals of the United States
                    Government in regard to that matter were communicated to you in my note of the
                    17th instant.<anchor n="10" xml:id="d157-f2"/></p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>(For the Secretary of State),<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">G. H.
                            Villiers</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
